{"id":"8e3c4e75-f145-4649-a11d-80b6e3d4d9a8","expr":"result >= 0 && result <= 255","rationale":"The method decodes two hex digits into a byte value, thus result is in the 0-255 range.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"io.netty.util.internal.StringUtil#decodeHexByte(CharSequence,int):byte","file":"io/netty/util/internal/StringUtil.java","createdAt":"2026-08-31T05:08:39.907070189Z"}
{"id":"3ba4f378-83c4-4958-a6f7-1c03ca70a9ee","expr":"length >= 0 && (length & 1) == 0","rationale":"The method throws if length is negative or odd, so at entry length is non-negative and even.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"io.netty.util.internal.StringUtil#decodeHexDump(CharSequence,int,int):byte[]","file":"io/netty/util/internal/StringUtil.java","createdAt":"2026-08-31T05:08:39.913760269Z"}
{"id":"add84c2f-496a-4b1f-9ff1-d6c0608f0312","expr":"hexDump != null","rationale":"For safe indexing and decoding, hexDump must be non-null.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"io.netty.util.internal.StringUtil#decodeHexDump(CharSequence,int,int):byte[]","file":"io/netty/util/internal/StringUtil.java","createdAt":"2026-08-31T05:08:39.913760269Z"}
{"id":"13b0bb43-c5f8-4dce-9c51-a86dc4aee3e9","expr":"fromIndex >= 0","rationale":"The fromIndex parameter is usually non-negative as an index offset.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"io.netty.util.internal.StringUtil#decodeHexDump(CharSequence,int,int):byte[]","file":"io/netty/util/internal/StringUtil.java","createdAt":"2026-08-31T05:08:39.913760269Z"}
{"id":"8a52e7cc-9e7a-44af-b612-2878ec0abf78","expr":"fromIndex + length <= hexDump.length()","rationale":"The slice of hexDump from fromIndex to fromIndex + length must be within bounds.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"io.netty.util.internal.StringUtil#decodeHexDump(CharSequence,int,int):byte[]","file":"io/netty/util/internal/StringUtil.java","createdAt":"2026-08-31T05:08:39.913760269Z"}
{"id":"7a74da28-eb86-49f6-a576-18e89a42f4ca","expr":"hexDump != null && hexDump.length() % 2 == 0","rationale":"Hex dumps typically have even length as each pair of characters represents one byte.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"io.netty.util.internal.StringUtil#decodeHexDump(CharSequence):byte[]","file":"io/netty/util/internal/StringUtil.java","createdAt":"2026-08-31T05:08:39.915120278Z"}
{"id":"e1985ee8-de2b-4242-bd34-b88b228889f2","expr":"hexDump.length() >= 0","rationale":"CharSequence length is always >= 0.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"io.netty.util.internal.StringUtil#decodeHexDump(CharSequence):byte[]","file":"io/netty/util/internal/StringUtil.java","createdAt":"2026-08-31T05:08:39.915120278Z"}
{"id":"00ed1171-3e61-499f-ab9f-d2bfb5f571ec","expr":"hexDump.length() == 0 || hexDump.length() % 2 == 0","rationale":"Empty hex dump or hex dump with even length is expected.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"io.netty.util.internal.StringUtil#decodeHexDump(CharSequence):byte[]","file":"io/netty/util/internal/StringUtil.java","createdAt":"2026-08-31T05:08:39.915120278Z"}
{"id":"928fb012-6653-4d15-9ac1-00bdbe40ecd4","expr":"result >= 0 && result <= 15 && (b >= 0 && b < 128)","rationale":"Result corresponds to a decoded hex nibble between 0 and 15 for input byte b in valid range.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"io.netty.util.internal.StringUtil#decodeHexNibble(byte):int","file":"io/netty/util/internal/StringUtil.java","createdAt":"2026-08-31T05:08:39.916735789Z"}
{"id":"d7c65b58-96ae-4916-a823-b252235cc765","expr":"! (result < 0) || (b < 0 || b >= 128)","rationale":"Negative result indicates b is outside valid ASCII range for hex parsing.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"io.netty.util.internal.StringUtil#decodeHexNibble(byte):int","file":"io/netty/util/internal/StringUtil.java","createdAt":"2026-08-31T05:08:39.916735789Z"}
{"id":"748c83b0-602c-4b1e-aa9c-48a2e1f5d89b","expr":"(b >= 48 && b <= 57) || (b >= 65 && b <= 70) || (b >= 97 && b <= 102) || result == -1","rationale":"If b is a valid hex digit byte, result is decoded value; otherwise result is -1.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"io.netty.util.internal.StringUtil#decodeHexNibble(byte):int","file":"io/netty/util/internal/StringUtil.java","createdAt":"2026-08-31T05:08:39.916735789Z"}
{"id":"0d6c9b7d-be7d-4b9f-8b44-48df4a698028","expr":"result == (b >= 48 && b <= 57 ? b - 48 : (b >= 65 && b <= 70 ? b - 55 : (b >= 97 && b <= 102 ? b - 87 : -1)))","rationale":"Result equals the numerical hex value decoded from ASCII digit or letter b, or -1 for invalid.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"io.netty.util.internal.StringUtil#decodeHexNibble(byte):int","file":"io/netty/util/internal/StringUtil.java","createdAt":"2026-08-31T05:08:39.916735789Z"}
{"id":"d5bb8057-d8f7-46e3-a0d9-e8820ed009ee","expr":"result != -1 || (b < 48 || (b > 57 && b < 65) || (b > 70 && b < 97) || b > 102)","rationale":"If result is -1, then b is outside all ranges of ASCII hex digit characters.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"io.netty.util.internal.StringUtil#decodeHexNibble(byte):int","file":"io/netty/util/internal/StringUtil.java","createdAt":"2026-08-31T05:08:39.916735789Z"}
{"id":"4b57ff8f-c6e0-45b3-b7a8-974ea9385728","expr":"result != null && result.length == hexDump.length() / 2 || hexDump.length() % 2 == 1 || hexDump.length() == 0","rationale":"If the input hexDump has an even length, result length should be half that length because each pair of hex characters corresponds to one byte.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"io.netty.util.internal.StringUtil#decodeHexDump(CharSequence):byte[]","file":"io/netty/util/internal/StringUtil.java","createdAt":"2026-08-31T05:08:39.918028461Z"}
{"id":"86d764fa-508c-420d-8fc0-65b696a9b05e","expr":"result != null","rationale":"The method returns a byte array, so result should not be null.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"io.netty.util.internal.StringUtil#decodeHexDump(CharSequence):byte[]","file":"io/netty/util/internal/StringUtil.java","createdAt":"2026-08-31T05:08:39.918028461Z"}
{"id":"0023d40d-60b3-4fa3-ad71-c0ab62654f85","expr":"(hexDump.length() % 2 == 0) == (result.length == hexDump.length() / 2)","rationale":"When hexDump length is even, result length equals exactly half the length of hexDump.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"io.netty.util.internal.StringUtil#decodeHexDump(CharSequence):byte[]","file":"io/netty/util/internal/StringUtil.java","createdAt":"2026-08-31T05:08:39.918028461Z"}
